{
  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) at 0.591 acc, showing that multiprofile + avgpool aggregation is the strongest RNA configuration, and pca_n2000 outperforms scgpt. Image-only (resnet50) is very weak (0.208), but it is untested whether image features provide complementary signal when fused with the strong RNA representation. Question: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) directly extends config_002 by adding the image modality with the simplest fusion (concat), isolating the effect of multimodal fusion while keeping all other settings identical to the best RNA-only baseline. Why this experiment: With only 4 experiments remaining, this is the highest-information next step. If multimodal fusion improves on 0.591, we can then explore better image encoders (ViT-L) and fusion strategies (weighted) in the remaining budget. If it does not improve, we confirm RNA-only is sufficient and can focus remaining experiments on RNA encoder variants (e.g., scvi_n200) or accept the current best. This avoids changing multiple variables at once and gives a clean binary signal about whether the image modality is worth further investment."
}

